>>__ load "simpExtLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `split_ss`

``` hol4
simpExtLib.split_ss : simpExtLib.ssfrag
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Splits datatype case expressions and registered split rules during extension
simplification. The fragment is named `"split"`; its `"splitter"` looper uses
TypeBase rules for fully applied case constants in the goal, and persistent
`split` rules when explicitly enabled. It also rewrites
`(b ==> t) /\ (~b ==> t)` to `t`.

Loading the fragment does not register the attribute or theorem set. Without
initialization, TypeBase and local `Split` rules still work. Persistent
registration must precede replay: exporting theories load `splitPersistLib`
and record it with `Theory.add_ML_dependency` on the earliest split-bearing
theory. Ancestor additions and `splitLib.exclude_split` removals then replay
on fresh import; see `splitLib.enable_split_attribute` for ordering.

`ExclX "split:thy$name"` suppresses an attribute rule for one invocation;
`ExclX "case:ty"` suppresses datatype splits.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>> val c = Context.snapshot();
>>_ val ext_bool_ss = simpExtLib.lift_simpset boolSimps.bool_ss;
>>_ val ss = simpExtLib.++ (ext_bool_ss,simpExtLib.split_ss);
>> simpExtLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC {safe = false} ss []
     ([], “P (if b then 1 else 2) : bool”) c;
>> simpExtLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC {safe = false} ss
     [simpExtLib.ExclX "case:bool"] ([], “P (if b then 1 else 2) : bool”) c;
```

